## Checker-forced compromises (noted per §Verify instruction)
1. 016 "1. sorrendje": the reviewer's "első sorrendje" removes the digit that the ko source carries as 제1순위,
   and the R11 lexical exemption only covers 제3자/제3국/N심 — the checker FAILed with
   `numbers FAIL missing from translation (2): 1×2`. Final wording: "a törvényes öröklés 1. sorrendű örökösei"
   (keeps the digit, still idiomatic legal Hungarian).
2. 015 §"telephely előzetes lekérdezése": "2023. január 1-jétől …" at the start of a line is parsed by the
   markdown block counter as an ordered-list marker (`blocks FAIL list items 0 → 1`). The sentence was recast so
   the date is mid-sentence; block count restored.
3. Two Hungarian words were rejected by the `nationality` lane because they contain the substring "magyar"
   ("magyarázni" in 002, "a magyar jogi nyelv" in 007). Reworded ("értelmezni", "ennek a szülői felügyelet
   fogalma felel meg"). Note: "magyarul"/"magyar nyelven" are whitelisted, plain "magyar" is not.
4. b#12 (ROC year gloss in 010) adds the year 2020, which the checker reports as an extra number — that is a WARN,
   not a FAIL; 010 still PASSes.

